 ludo:['Boards','CPU or local 2-player','BRING ALL FOUR HOME','Four tokens each. Six to enter and roll again; exact roll to finish. Start squares are safe. This classic preset has no blockades, capture bonus or three-sixes penalty. Computer opponent by default; local two-player in settings.'],
 counters:['Street','CPU or local 2-player','BOTTLE TOPS. REAL TOUCH.','Choose a cap and aim at the pebble ball. Hold Flick to control force. E changes cap. First to three goals, or highest score after 24 flicks. Play against the computer or select local two-player in settings.'],
 kpitinge:['Skill','Weighted-peg toss','PLANT THE POINT.','Aim left/right and release the weighted practice peg near vertical. Its actual flight, landing location and orientation decide whether it plants in the sand mound. Five attempts; points replace forfeits.'],
 alasa:['Skill','Seed-flick duel','FIVE SEEDS EACH.','Take turns with the computer flicking star-apple-shaped seeds into a small hole. Aim left/right or tap the ground. Hold Flick to set force; E changes the preset. Only seeds sunk count. Five seeds each.'],
 numbers:['Compound','Quick-response circle','YOUR TURN. THINK QUICK.','Players name prime numbers in turn. Choose a prime before the response window closes. Wrong or late answers leave the circle. Eight turns get progressively quicker; the time windows and numeric choices are digital conventions.'],
 chempe:['Compound','Food-holder & claimant','REMEMBER WHO CALLS WHAT.','Alternate roles. When food appears, the food-holder calls “No Chem pe!” to keep the exemption; the claimant calls “Chempε!” first to request equal sharing. Six reflex exchanges. The timing contest is an optional arcade adaptation.'],
 pempenaa:['Rhythm','Leg-counting game','FOLLOW THE PHRASE.','Four seated players extend both legs. The count moves across the remaining legs. At phrase-end, the selected leg folds. When your leg is selected, choose left or right. The first with both legs folded ranks first. Phrase lengths are an arcade convention.'],
 mbobagor:['Rhythm','Shared stone rhythm','ONE STONE FOR EACH PLAYER.','Six seated players each pass a stone anticlockwise on the shared clap. Press Pass on the beat. Missing a transfer leaves an extra stone in your pile. Sixteen passes wins; three piled stones end this arcade round.'],
